Here’s a quick way you can pull out only those items whose **`data‑active`** flag is set to `true`.  
Just feed your existing `listElement` into the helper below (the function name comes straight from the toolbox you shared):

```js
// Assuming `listElement` already holds the DOM node / array you’re working with:
const activeItems = getActiveDataEntries({
  listElement,          // <-- the element/array you passed earlier
  attribute: 'data-active', // optional – defaults to “data-active”
  value: true            // optional – defaults to true
});

console.log(activeItems); // → Array of elements where data-active === true
```

If you prefer not to specify the parameters explicitly, you can rely entirely on their defaults:

```js
const activeItems = getActiveDataEntries({ listElement });
```

Either approach returns an array containing *only* the entries marked as active (`data-active="true"`).
